; Regression for PR.md 2.3: Lambda strings are length-tagged, but fopen took
; the bytes as a C string, so a path with an embedded NUL silently truncated
; to its prefix and wrote the prefix file.  Embedded NULs must be rejected by
; returning the normal write-file failure value (-1) instead.
; (u0000 is the Lambda string escape for an embedded NUL.)
(write-file "regr_nul_path.tmp\u0000suffix" (arrayb 2 65))
